window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Sometimes the wrong side could be the right side.</p> <p>My father never loved me.</p> <p>I was never good enough for him because I was different.</p> <p>My differences made me vulnerable to his cruelty, and a mistake I made brought a deeper level of hell into my life.</p> <p>When my curiosity got the better of me one night, it ended with me being forced out of the world I’d learned to exist in before I was thrust into another.</p> <p>This new world is darker and more dangerous.</p> <p>It’s filled with lies, deceit, and pain.</p> <p>I have rules I live by now because the wicked walk these halls.</p> <p>1) Never underestimate the level of a monster’s depravity.</p> <p>2) Never take anything at face value.</p> <p>3) Fight, always, even if you’re doing it from the shadows.</p> <p>4) Remember everything…Because they will, and they will use it against you.</p> <p>If I have to play the twisted games at Chapel Crest, I will.</p> <p>For now.</p> <p>They just need to understand, the darkness comes for us all, and I’m the king of it.</p> <p>Shadow is book 4.5 in The Boys of Chapel Crest and should be listened to after Sinful. Please check author’s note for warnings.</p>"; 
